1
00:00:00,450 --> 00:00:04,384
We are Team Huzzards, and this is our answer to SIH26121.

2
00:00:04,984 --> 00:00:08,009
Drilling engineers make decisions at the bit — in minutes.

3
00:00:08,109 --> 00:00:12,676
But what nearby wells faced at this exact depth — losses, stuck pipe,

4
00:00:12,716 --> 00:00:14,668
kicks — is buried in thousands of reports.

5
00:00:14,768 --> 00:00:19,396
Unplanned events like these can eat ten to twenty percent of a well's time — and they repeat.

6
00:00:21,159 --> 00:00:24,224
Meet NWIS — the Nearby Wells Intelligence System.

7
00:00:24,312 --> 00:00:27,822
It sits beside eRTMAC and connects the bit's depth to what nearby wells learned there:

8
00:00:27,862 --> 00:00:32,566
what happened, why, what worked — and the report page that proves it.

9
00:00:32,646 --> 00:00:36,922
Not a dashboard. Not a chatbot. The memory of the field — when it matters.

10
00:00:38,222 --> 00:00:40,516
The core innovation is a depth-aware link.

11
00:00:41,077 --> 00:00:45,085
As the bit drills, NWIS finds the offset wells that had trouble at that depth,

12
00:00:45,125 --> 00:00:47,199
and streams their evidence to the active well.

13
00:00:48,227 --> 00:00:51,133
Every alert is explainable, every sentence is cited

14
00:00:51,173 --> 00:00:55,272
and a learned model cross-checks each score, without ever overriding the engineer.

15
00:00:56,824 --> 00:00:58,486
This is the Command Center: well OIL-AX-102,

16
00:00:58,526 --> 00:01:02,219
drilling the Barail Group at 3,100 metres.

17
00:01:03,747 --> 00:01:08,419
Wellbore, live parameters, field map and risk radar — all driven by one depth.

18
00:01:09,588 --> 00:01:10,855
Let's start drilling.

19
00:01:12,823 --> 00:01:17,176
At 3,150 metres, NWIS raises a mud-loss alert — before the losses begin.

20
00:01:17,982 --> 00:01:19,847
Two offsets lost returns right here,

21
00:01:19,887 --> 00:01:22,362
and the ECD is climbing toward their loss point.

22
00:01:22,441 --> 00:01:26,550
Switch to Subsurface: the rock layers come from every offset's formation tops,

23
00:01:26,590 --> 00:01:30,007
with true well paths and past incidents glowing at their depth.

24
00:01:32,469 --> 00:01:37,111
At 3,380 metres, the stuck-pipe alert fires — and the evidence streams to the bit.

25
00:01:37,192 --> 00:01:40,925
Click Why, and the alert shows its working: every factor, every signal,

26
00:01:40,965 --> 00:01:43,362
every supporting well — and what to check next.

27
00:01:43,566 --> 00:01:47,882
The Well Intelligence page opens any offset: its drilling parameters against ours,

28
00:01:47,922 --> 00:01:50,581
depth for depth, beside every event and lesson.

29
00:01:50,682 --> 00:01:52,527
Compare correlates formation tops,

30
00:01:52,567 --> 00:01:56,266
casing and mud weights across the offsets — so the differences stand out.

31
00:01:56,370 --> 00:01:59,734
Ask in plain English — every sentence of the answer is cited,

32
00:01:59,774 --> 00:02:01,987
and one click opens the original report page.

33
00:02:05,442 --> 00:02:06,404
For the shift handover,

34
00:02:06,444 --> 00:02:09,679
the look-ahead brief turns the next 300 metres into one page:

35
00:02:09,754 --> 00:02:12,940
hazards, what worked fastest, the mud-weight window

36
00:02:12,980 --> 00:02:17,197
and 8.8 hours of expected NPT, about eleven lakh rupees at stake.

37
00:02:17,458 --> 00:02:19,562
Even scanned reports are read with OCR and turned into events

38
00:02:19,602 --> 00:02:22,498
and nothing is saved until an engineer approves it.

39
00:02:27,956 --> 00:02:29,099
And it's not just a demo:

40
00:02:29,139 --> 00:02:33,501
we ran the same pipeline on 1,970 real well histories from the Norwegian shelf

41
00:02:33,573 --> 00:02:35,178
611 drilling problems found in seconds,

42
00:02:35,218 --> 00:02:39,319
94 percent correct on wells it had never seen.

43
00:02:41,669 --> 00:02:44,575
In our demo field, the offsets lost 110 hours in the three windows ahead

44
00:02:44,615 --> 00:02:48,332
NWIS flagged every one before the bit got there.

45
00:02:48,432 --> 00:02:50,396
Connected to eRTMAC and Oil India's archive, every rig,

46
00:02:50,436 --> 00:02:54,934
every handover and every new engineer gets the field's memory.

47
00:02:55,084 --> 00:02:58,295
NWIS. Know what's below — before you drill it.
